<span id="A5.p5.pic1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p">The search results list William Garland “Bill” Dailey, a relief pitcher born in Arlington County, Virginia, on May 13, 1935. That matches the birthplace and 1930s birth-year clues. I now need to confirm that he had a mid-century season in which he recorded “nearly twenty” saves and finished third in the league, and then determine the team with which he made his major-league debut. I’ll open his Wikipedia page to verify these details.</span>
